1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,000
NeXus is an AI doctor for physical hardware, powered by NVIDIA Nemotron on Nebius.

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:30,000
This real ESP32-S3 platform has protected power, current sensing, two motor drivers, three encoder motors, PS2 control, and an emergency stop.

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:47,000
A versioned JSON profile defines every component, pin, connection, limit, and telemetry field.

4
00:00:47,000 --> 00:01:05,000
NeXus verifies firmware and sensor identity, stores serial telemetry, and reports signal faults separately from a powered-off rail.

5
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Each wheel has independent RPM evidence. Releasing the controller returns the vehicle to fail-safe stop.

6
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:42,000
The Hardware Graph and wiring guide expose the same machine-readable topology to people and agents.

7
00:01:42,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Nemotron receives grounded context and allowlisted tools, ranks hypotheses, and explains the next safe step.

8
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Deterministic policy controls every action. The audit timeline records proposal, approval or rejection, execution, and verification.

9
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:47,000
Recovery requires a newer sample. Manual and Auto Treatment never hide missing safety conditions.

10
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:55,000
NeXus reduces hardware guesswork without giving AI unsafe authority.
